# Next.js static export output + build metadata - regenerated by every
# `pnpm build`/`next build` run (including FLEET_WATCH.ps1's own local
# auto-deploy gate), never a tracked source artifact. Missing until now
# - found because it kept leaving apps/web/out untracked after every
# build, which blocked the auto-deploy's own working-tree-clean check
# on its very next cycle.
apps/web/out/
apps/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo

# FLEET_WATCH.ps1 local state files - harness-local, never a tracked
# artifact (would otherwise dirty the working tree and block the
# auto-deploy's own clean-tree pre-check on the very next cycle).
.fleet-watch-state.json
.fleet-deploy-state.json
.fleet-trigger-daemon-log.json
.fleet-trigger-daemon-log.ndjson

# New fleet runner state, leases, event streams, and transient Python data.
# Python bytecode/cache patterns are already covered globally above.
.fleet-runtime/

# W-98 follow-up (2026-09-08): Write-FleetSchedule's actual write call
# has now been removed from scripts/FLEET_WATCH.ps1 entirely (not just
# gitignored) per the operator's explicit follow-up ask - this entry
# stays as defense-in-depth in case a stray copy of the file exists
# locally on a machine that ran an older version of the script, not
# because anything still writes it.
docs/FLEET_SCHEDULE.md

# W-98 follow-up (2026-09-08): apps/artifacts/ and apps/web/artifacts/
# are real, untracked headless-proof/screenshot output (confirmed via
# git status - apps/artifacts/w63/live-fullscreen-1366.png is a real
# file) with no in-repo generator script found to relocate instead -
# same dirty-working-tree-guard-trip class as every other entry in
# this section.
apps/artifacts/
apps/web/artifacts/

# Housekeeping (2026-09-09, SCRIBE): graphify's knowledge-graph index
# output (~1.4MB JSON) is a local build artifact, confirmed showing as
# untracked noise in main's git status - never meant to enter Git,
# same dirty-working-tree-guard-trip class as the entries above.
graphify-out/
apps/graphify-out/
